    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, led by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** occupies the top spot in our lineup projections; he benefits from a favorable matchup against a neutral pitcher and a high-efficiency environment where his ability to capitalize on a slow delivery (85% SB potential) makes him an elite asset for our scarce speed category. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a top-tier start despite his assumed #8 spot in the order; the massive 19% SP skill advantage and a favorable wind-out condition in a hitter-friendly park elevate his floor significantly, offsetting the downside of his bottom-order placement. **Nasim Nunez** (71.66) also warrants attention, as the same park factors and SP matchup offer substantial value for a bottom-of-the-order bat.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational risks, most notably a 33% rain risk impacting **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Nasim Nunez**. While these players are currently recommended, their game status should be monitored closely. The most difficult decision rested with **Gunnar Henderson** (58.32), who narrowly missed the starting cut. Despite his raw talent, the optimizer penalized **Gunnar Henderson** significantly due to a negative platoon split against a tough left-handed arm, Eduardo Rivera. Ultimately, the algorithm prioritized the more favorable matchups and platoon dynamics of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Jacob Wilson** to maximize our daily efficiency score. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (57.32) remains a start despite facing an elite arm in Zack Wheeler; his base projection is resilient enough that his presence in the lineup is justified despite the challenging 2.99 xERA matchup.",
